# Regex replace capture group expansion

Verifies replacement strings expand capture groups: numbered groups swap the
two words of `hello world`, and named groups reformat the hyphenated pair in
`foo-bar`.

>>> source
const swapped: string = "hello world"->replace(/(\w+) (\w+)/, "$2 $1")
print(swapped)
const named: string = "foo-bar"->replace(/(?P<first>\w+)-(?P<second>\w+)/g, "$second:$first")
print(named)

<<< stdout
world hello
bar:foo

<<< stderr
